cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HydraMind in your research or projects, please cite it as below."
title: "HydraMind: trust-weighted graph memory for coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HydraMind contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/himanshu748/hydramind"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - agent-memory
  - knowledge-graph
  - graph-database
  - hydradb
  - provenance
  - trust
abstract: >-
  HydraMind is an MCP server that gives coding agents persistent memory in a
  HydraDB graph. It records contradictions, revisions, and provenance as
  relationships, propagates lost trust through derived memories, and abstains
  when evidence is insufficient.
